  "solution": "Given:\n\n5sqrt{3} + sqrt{75} = 17.32\n\nCalculation:\n\n5sqrt{3} + sqrt{75} = 17.32\n\n⇒ 5sqrt{3} + 5sqrt{3} = 17.32\n\n⇒ 10sqrt{3} = 17.32\n\n⇒ sqrt{3} = 17.32/10\n\n⇒ sqrt{3} = 1.732 ....(1)\n\nNow,\n\n14sqrt{3} + sqrt{108}\n\n⇒ 14sqrt{3} + sqrt{36 × 3}\n\n⇒ 14sqrt{3} + 6sqrt{3}\n\n⇒ 20sqrt{3}\n\n⇒ 20 × 1.732 (From 1)\n\n⇒ 34.64\n\n**∴ The value of 14sqrt{3} + sqrt{108} is 34.64.**",
